# Badger Architecture

Current Stable Components

- CLI
- Tunnel Server
- Tunnel Protocol
- Local Proxy
- Request Forwarder
- Tunnel Manager
- Event Bus (`packages/shared/src/event-bus` — typed publish/subscribe)
- Traffic Recorder (`apps/server/src/traffic` — EventBus subscriber, in-memory store)
- Dashboard scaffold (`apps/dashboard` — Next.js 16, no product UI yet)

Stable Contracts

- Tunnel protocol messages
- CLI commands
- WebSocket protocol
- Public URL generation
- EventBus interface and `BadgerEventType` payloads (`@hridhin-k/badger-shared/event-bus`)
- Dashboard ↔ Server boundary: public REST + WebSocket only
- `TrafficRecordStore` persistence port

Future Modules

- Inspector
- Dashboard UI screens
- AI Engine
- Plugin SDK

Rules

Never rewrite stable modules.

New features must be added as separate modules.

Prefer composition through interfaces.

Avoid coupling new modules directly to forwarding logic.

Prefer events over direct service calls.

Lifecycle emissions must be fire-and-forget and must never alter tunnel control flow.
See [docs/event-bus.md](../../docs/event-bus.md).

The Dashboard must never import server internals.
See [docs/dashboard.md](../../docs/dashboard.md).
